   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## starter 08 \u00b7 moving pieces\n\n**You need:** Blender 4.x. No AI models.\n\n**Your own model:** paste the path of your .blend / .fbx / .obj / .abc / .glb / .usd into `file` of **scene render** (Explorer: right click the file, Copy as path). Empty = the sample building.\n\n**Do:** Queue. Every stone, window frame and voussoir of the sample model is a piece. A band runs across the facade\n(falloff: pulse, left to right, looping every 4 s), the pieces it reaches are pushed out of the wall and turn a little, then\ncome back. Cycles renders 4 seconds from an audience spot; the first run takes about a minute, a changed setting\nrenders only what changed.\n\n**Then try:** falloff `type = stagger` with `direction = from the centre`; a second transform chained after the first\n(they add up) with its own falloff `noise`; `look = projected matrix` with an image on `matrix` (the picture is cast\nfrom the projector onto the moving pieces); `view = projector` for the frames you would actually project.\nWith regions connected to scene pieces (starter 07) and `source = regions: one piece each`, whole windows or floors move\nas one block; **pieces beat falloff** makes them jump on the beats of the director's timeline.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
